through the point $(0,0)$ in the $xy$-plane, and is\n\n- bounded below by $z=0=0,$ and\n\n- bounded above by $z=3=3.$\n\nAs a result, in cylindrical polar coordinates, our region can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\Delta=\\{(r,\\theta,z):0\\le r\\le 4,\\ 0\\le\\theta<2\\cdot \\pi,\\ 0\\le z\\le 3\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\iiint_R \\sqrt{(x)^{2}+(y)^{2}}\\,dV &=\\iiint_\\Delta (\\sqrt{(r\\cdot \\cos(\\theta))^2+(r\\cdot \\sin(\\theta))^2})\\cdot r\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{2\\cdot \\pi}\\int_0^{4}\\int_{0}^{3}(r)^{2}\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{2\\cdot \\pi}\\int_0^{4}(r)^{2}[z]_{z=0}^{z=3}\\,dr\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{2\\cdot \\pi}\\int_0^{4}(r)^{2}((3)-(0))\\,dr\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{2\\cdot \\pi}\\int_0^{4}3\\cdot (r)^{2}\\,dr\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{2\\cdot \\pi}[(r)^{3}]_{r=0}^{r=4}\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{2\\cdot \\pi}(((4))^{3})-(((0))^{3})\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{2\\cdot \\pi}(64)-(0)\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{2\\cdot \\pi}64\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=[64\\cdot \\theta]_{\\theta=0}^{\\theta=2\\cdot \\pi} \\\\ &=(128\\cdot \\pi)-(0) \\\\ &=128\\cdot \\pi\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["57e8e949-e40f-5a5f-a5fb-3d827a224266"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "d68b09e5-524b-56e8-8b3e-d922ab80c8e3" :answer/id #uuid "d68b09e5-524b-56e8-8b3e-d922ab80c8e3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "66\\cdot \\pi" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "66af9ffc-ae30-5a4e-8b1b-228331e6b034" :answer/id #uuid "66af9ffc-ae30-5a4e-8b1b-228331e6b034" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "42\\cdot \\pi" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "646cbcae-95be-5a16-90c4-402ea2065742" :answer/id #uuid "646cbcae-95be-5a16-90c4-402ea2065742" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "84\\cdot \\pi" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "237c1dc0-9a08-5feb-9f93-69378beb0d5a" :answer/id #uuid "237c1dc0-9a08-5feb-9f93-69378beb0d5a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "252\\cdot \\pi" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "bab2ee4a-610e-5302-bcd4-2e5229f07fb7" :answer/id #uuid "bab2ee4a-610e-5302-bcd4-2e5229f07fb7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "168\\cdot \\pi" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "424213bf-d747-5c2b-8b1c-17e303286030" :answer-field/id #uuid "424213bf-d747-5c2b-8b1c-17e303286030" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["d68b09e5-524b-56e8-8b3e-d922ab80c8e3" "66af9ffc-ae30-5a4e-8b1b-228331e6b034" "646cbcae-95be-5a16-90c4-402ea2065742" "237c1dc0-9a08-5feb-9f93-69378beb0d5a" "bab2ee4a-610e-5302-bcd4-2e5229f07fb7"] :answer-field/correct "646cbcae-95be-5a16-90c4-402ea2065742" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "74a2b9bd-8d96-5a52-868d-e97a9b8e01c9" :question/id #uuid "74a2b9bd-8d96-5a52-868d-e97a9b8e01c9" :question/problem "Evaluate the triple integral\n\n$$\n\\iiint_R 2\\cdot z\\cdot ((x)^{2}+(y)^{2})^{-\\frac{1}{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}V\n$$\n\nover the region $R$ enclosed inside the cylinder $x^2+y^2=9$ and between the surfaces $z=0$ and $z=\\sqrt{-(x)^{2}+(y)^{2}+14}.$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n\\iiint_R f(x,y,z)\\,dV=\\iiint_\\Delta f(r\\cos\\theta,r\\sin\\theta,z)\\,r\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta.\n$$\n\nIf $(r,\\theta,z)$ are the cylindrical polar coordinates of a point, then its Cartesian coordinates $(x,y,z)$ can be found by using the formulas\n\n$$\nx=r\\cos\\theta,\\quad y=r\\sin\\theta,\\quad z=z.\n$$\n\nFirst, let's sketch the projection of $R$ onto the $xy$-plane:\n\n![](images/8e/8ee9b491452a26902c4800a006c16f1bbca31f0e800ec9aad20dfeef68eed8f4.png)\n\nThe region $R$ is a right vertical cylinder of radius $3$ whose axis passes through the point $(0,0)$ in the $xy$-plane, and is\n\n- bounded below by $z=0=0,$ and\n\n- bounded above by $z=\\sqrt{-(x)^{2}+(y)^{2}+14}=\\sqrt{-(r)^{2}\\cdot \\cos(2\\cdot \\theta)+14}.$\n\nAs a result, in cylindrical polar coordinates, our region can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\Delta=\\{(r,\\theta,z):0\\le r\\le 3,\\ 0\\le\\theta<2\\cdot \\pi,\\ 0\\le z\\le \\sqrt{-(r)^{2}\\cdot \\cos(2\\cdot \\theta)+14}\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\iiint_R 2\\cdot z\\cdot ((x)^{2}+(y)^{2})^{-\\frac{1}{2}}\\,dV &=\\iiint_\\Delta (2\\cdot \\frac{z}{\\sqrt{(r\\cdot \\cos(\\theta))^2+(r\\cdot \\sin(\\theta))^2}})\\cdot r\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{2\\cdot \\pi}\\int_0^{3}\\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{-(r)^{2}\\cdot \\cos(2\\cdot \\theta)+14}}2\\cdot z\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{2\\cdot \\pi}\\int_0^{3}[(z)^{2}]_{z=0}^{z=\\sqrt{-(r)^{2}\\cdot \\cos(2\\cdot \\theta)+14}}\\,dr\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{2\\cdot \\pi}\\int_0^{3}(((\\sqrt{-(r)^{2}\\cdot \\cos(2\\cdot \\theta)+14}))^{2})-(((0))^{2})\\,dr\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{2\\cdot \\pi}\\int_0^{3}-(r)^{2}\\cdot \\cos(2\\cdot \\theta)+14\\,dr\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{2\\cdot \\pi}[-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot (r)^{3}\\cdot \\cos(2\\cdot \\theta)+14\\cdot r]_{r=0}^{r=3}\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{2\\cdot \\pi}(-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot ((3))^{3}\\cdot \\cos(2\\cdot \\theta))-(-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot ((0))^{3}\\cdot \\cos(2\\cdot \\theta))+(14\\cdot (3))-(14\\cdot (0))\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{2\\cdot \\pi}(-9\\cdot \\cos(2\\cdot \\theta))-(0)+(42)-(0)\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{2\\cdot \\pi}42-9\\cdot \\cos(2\\cdot \\theta)\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=[42\\cdot \\theta-9\\cdot \\cos(\\theta)\\cdot \\sin(\\theta)]_{\\theta=0}^{\\theta=2\\cdot \\pi} \\\\ &=(84\\cdot \\pi)-(0)+(0)-(0) \\\\ &=84\\cdot \\pi\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["424213bf-d747-5c2b-8b1c-17e303286030"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "fc158f8d-2987-5499-a8ed-77f033124c1b" :answer/id #uuid "fc158f8d-2987-5499-a8ed-77f033124c1b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\cdot \\pi" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "b062a522-6a46-5f79-9299-18183553eb22" :answer/id #uuid "b062a522-6a46-5f79-9299-18183553eb22" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot \\pi" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "9ebd6dd6-7259-5120-97a3-66b51aeb5bdb" :answer/id #uuid "9ebd6dd6-7259-5120-97a3-66b51aeb5bdb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12\\cdot \\pi" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "ac6c862a-55e0-54f9-b7f6-7a2dc48c416c" :answer/id #uuid "ac6c862a-55e0-54f9-b7f6-7a2dc48c416c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1+3\\cdot \\pi" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "f9945e02-9035-5167-8318-4361e517c387" :answer/id #uuid "f9945e02-9035-5167-8318-4361e517c387" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}\\cdot \\pi" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "14d2c317-5999-5ae3-83ba-55833a642212" :answer-field/id #uuid "14d2c317-5999-5ae3-83ba-55833a642212" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["fc158f8d-2987-5499-a8ed-77f033124c1b" "b062a522-6a46-5f79-9299-18183553eb22" "9ebd6dd6-7259-5120-97a3-66b51aeb5bdb" "ac6c862a-55e0-54f9-b7f6-7a2dc48c416c" "f9945e02-9035-5167-8318-4361e517c387"] :answer-field/correct "fc158f8d-2987-5499-a8ed-77f033124c1b" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "3d825389-7a3e-5461-af4a-30fb0473dbe9" :question/id #uuid "3d825389-7a3e-5461-af4a-30fb0473dbe9" :question/problem "Evaluate the triple integral\n\n$$\n\\iiint_R \\sqrt{(x)^{2}+(y)^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}V\n$$\n\nover the region $R$ enclosed inside the cylinder $x^2+y^2=1$ and between the surfaces $z=0$ and $z=9-2\\cdot y.$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n\\iiint_R f(x,y,z)\\,dV=\\iiint_\\Delta f(r\\cos\\theta,r\\sin\\theta,z)\\,r\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta.\n$$\n\nIf $(r,\\theta,z)$ are the cylindrical polar coordinates of a point, then its Cartesian coordinates $(x,y,z)$ can be found by using the formulas\n\n$$\nx=r\\cos\\theta,\\quad y=r\\sin\\theta,\\quad z=z.\n$$\n\nFirst, let's sketch the projection of $R$ onto the $xy$-plane:\n\n![](images/c7/c7fe69ab2583c066df73bbf6719e4c58fea1ed565e345bc62c11b7ebc779508b.png)\n\nThe region $R$ is a right vertical cylinder of radius $1$ whose axis passes through the point $(0,0)$ in the $xy$-plane, and is\n\n- bounded below by $z=0=0,$ and\n\n- bounded above by $z=9-2\\cdot y=-2\\cdot r\\cdot \\sin(\\theta)+9.$\n\nAs a result, in cylindrical polar coordinates, our region can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\Delta=\\{(r,\\theta,z):0\\le r\\le 1,\\ 0\\le\\theta<2\\cdot \\pi,\\ 0\\le z\\le -2\\cdot r\\cdot \\sin(\\theta)+9\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\iiint_R \\sqrt{(x)^{2}+(y)^{2}}\\,dV &=\\iiint_\\Delta (\\sqrt{(r\\cdot \\cos(\\theta))^2+(r\\cdot \\sin(\\theta))^2})\\cdot r\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{2\\cdot \\pi}\\int_0^{1}\\int_{0}^{-2\\cdot r\\cdot \\sin(\\theta)+9}(r)^{2}\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{2\\cdot \\pi}\\int_0^{1}(r)^{2}[z]_{z=0}^{z=-2\\cdot r\\cdot \\sin(\\theta)+9}\\,dr\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{2\\cdot \\pi}\\int_0^{1}(r)^{2}((-2\\cdot r\\cdot \\sin(\\theta)+9)-(0))\\,dr\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{2\\cdot \\pi}\\int_0^{1}-2\\cdot (r)^{3}\\cdot \\sin(\\theta)+9\\cdot (r)^{2}\\,dr\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{2\\cdot \\pi}[-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (r)^{4}\\cdot \\sin(\\theta)+3\\cdot (r)^{3}]_{r=0}^{r=1}\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{2\\cdot \\pi}(-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot ((1))^{4}\\cdot \\sin(\\theta))-(-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot ((0))^{4}\\cdot \\sin(\\theta))+(3\\cdot ((1))^{3})-(3\\cdot ((0))^{3})\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{2\\cdot \\pi}(-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\sin(\\theta))-(0)+(3)-(0)\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{2\\cdot \\pi}3-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\sin(\\theta)\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=[3\\cdot \\theta+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\cos(\\theta)]_{\\theta=0}^{\\theta=2\\cdot \\pi} \\\\ &=(6\\cdot \\pi)-(0)+(\\frac{1}{2})-(\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\ &=6\\cdot \\pi\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["14d2c317-5999-5ae3-83ba-55833a642212"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "db4ccc14-ea2a-521d-b14a-fa38d1435ac4" :answer/id #uuid "db4ccc14-ea2a-521d-b14a-fa38d1435ac4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-16+\\frac{40}{3}\\cdot \\pi\\cdot \\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "e84ef09f-1452-5309-a150-c450366b48f8" :answer/id #uuid "e84ef09f-1452-5309-a150-c450366b48f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "40\\cdot \\pi" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "a951bc16-7847-5502-a4f0-fe6ba9cfffa3" :answer/id #uuid "a951bc16-7847-5502-a4f0-fe6ba9cfffa3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{10}{3}\\cdot \\pi\\cdot \\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "4ef0905a-bdbf-5fea-9e69-8095deb48425" :answer/id #uuid "4ef0905a-bdbf-5fea-9e69-8095deb48425" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{160}{3}\\cdot \\pi\\cdot \\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "91eb5f07-47ff-5d2d-ace1-01e291591fe1" :answer/id #uuid "91eb5f07-47ff-5d2d-ace1-01e291591fe1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{80}{3}\\cdot \\pi\\cdot \\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "de2b82c7-fc0a-58d0-a814-18a367a7b7ea" :answer-field/id #uuid "de2b82c7-fc0a-58d0-a814-18a367a7b7ea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["db4ccc14-ea2a-521d-b14a-fa38d1435ac4" "e84ef09f-1452-5309-a150-c450366b48f8" "a951bc16-7847-5502-a4f0-fe6ba9cfffa3" "4ef0905a-bdbf-5fea-9e69-8095deb48425" "91eb5f07-47ff-5d2d-ace1-01e291591fe1"] :answer-field/correct "91eb5f07-47ff-5d2d-ace1-01e291591fe1" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "89c3ded2-ece5-51bf-a7d4-4718cdf0a70d" :question/id #uuid "89c3ded2-ece5-51bf-a7d4-4718cdf0a70d" :question/problem "Evaluate the triple integral\n\n$$\n\\iiint_R 4\\cdot \\sqrt{(x)^{2}+(y)^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}V\n$$\n\nover the region $R$ enclosed inside the cylinder $x^2+y^2=2$ and between the surfaces $z=0$ and $z=5-2\\cdot y.$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n\\iiint_R f(x,y,z)\\,dV=\\iiint_\\Delta f(r\\cos\\theta,r\\sin\\theta,z)\\,r\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta.\n$$\n\nIf $(r,\\theta,z)$ are the cylindrical polar coordinates of a point, then its Cartesian coordinates $(x,y,z)$ can be found by using the formulas\n\n$$\nx=r\\cos\\theta,\\quad y=r\\sin\\theta,\\quad z=z.\n$$\n\nFirst, let's sketch the projection of $R$ onto the $xy$-plane:\n\n![](images/c0/c015a0e708a8f931bc5d8857b69a734490518d79afb1f493183940f6d888ad1d.png)\n\nThe region $R$ is a right vertical cylinder of radius $\\sqrt{2}$ whose axis passes through the point $(0,0)$ in the $xy$-plane, and is\n\n- bounded below by $z=0=0,$ and\n\n- bounded above by $z=5-2\\cdot y=-2\\cdot r\\cdot \\sin(\\theta)+5.$\n\nAs a result, in cylindrical polar coordinates, our region can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\Delta=\\{(r,\\theta,z):0\\le r\\le \\sqrt{2},\\ 0\\le\\theta<2\\cdot \\pi,\\ 0\\le z\\le -2\\cdot r\\cdot \\sin(\\theta)+5\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\iiint_R 4\\cdot \\sqrt{(x)^{2}+(y)^{2}}\\,dV &=\\iiint_\\Delta (4\\cdot \\sqrt{(r\\cdot \\cos(\\theta))^2+(r\\cdot \\sin(\\theta))^2})\\cdot r\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{2\\cdot \\pi}\\int_0^{\\sqrt{2}}\\int_{0}^{-2\\cdot r\\cdot \\sin(\\theta)+5}4\\cdot (r)^{2}\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{2\\cdot \\pi}\\int_0^{\\sqrt{2}}4\\cdot (r)^{2}[z]_{z=0}^{z=-2\\cdot r\\cdot \\sin(\\theta)+5}\\,dr\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{2\\cdot \\pi}\\int_0^{\\sqrt{2}}4\\cdot (r)^{2}((-2\\cdot r\\cdot \\sin(\\theta)+5)-(0))\\,dr\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{2\\cdot \\pi}\\int_0^{\\sqrt{2}}-8\\cdot (r)^{3}\\cdot \\sin(\\theta)+20\\cdot (r)^{2}\\,dr\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{2\\cdot \\pi}[-2\\cdot (r)^{4}\\cdot \\sin(\\theta)+\\frac{20}{3}\\cdot (r)^{3}]_{r=0}^{r=\\sqrt{2}}\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{2\\cdot \\pi}(-2\\cdot ((\\sqrt{2}))^{4}\\cdot \\sin(\\theta))-(-2\\cdot ((0))^{4}\\cdot \\sin(\\theta))+(\\frac{20}{3}\\cdot ((\\sqrt{2}))^{3})-(\\frac{20}{3}\\cdot ((0))^{3})\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{2\\cdot \\pi}(-8\\cdot \\sin(\\theta))-(0)+(\\frac{40}{3}\\cdot \\sqrt{2})-(0)\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{2\\cdot \\pi}-8\\cdot \\sin(\\theta)+\\frac{40}{3}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=[\\frac{40}{3}\\cdot \\theta\\cdot \\sqrt{2}+8\\cdot \\cos(\\theta)]_{\\theta=0}^{\\theta=2\\cdot \\pi} \\\\ &=(\\frac{80}{3}\\cdot \\pi\\cdot \\sqrt{2})-(0)+(8)-(8) \\\\ &=\\frac{80}{3}\\cdot \\pi\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["de2b82c7-fc0a-58d0-a814-18a367a7b7ea"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "0a15b85a-ad02-5709-a268-9be5c6653c07" :answer/id #uuid "0a15b85a-ad02-5709-a268-9be5c6653c07" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "180\\cdot \\pi" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "ec96c562-7607-507f-9b9b-19e63a261a9a" :answer/id #uuid "ec96c562-7607-507f-9b9b-19e63a261a9a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{45}{8}\\cdot \\pi" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "f3b901ef-66b6-5561-805a-3f02727212c2" :answer/id #uuid "f3b901ef-66b6-5561-805a-3f02727212c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "90\\cdot \\pi" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "7b14ef7e-3f31-57b2-8f96-effeb4b7088d" :answer/id #uuid "7b14ef7e-3f31-57b2-8f96-effeb4b7088d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "72\\cdot \\pi\\cdot \\sqrt{6}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "99fc5045-61f5-50fa-a0e2-8f0003e56fa4" :answer/id #uuid "99fc5045-61f5-50fa-a0e2-8f0003e56fa4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "45\\cdot \\pi+200\\cdot \\sqrt{6}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "1b4a19c6-9237-53cb-b88d-eea0421ee991" :answer-field/id #uuid "1b4a19c6-9237-53cb-b88d-eea0421ee991" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["0a15b85a-ad02-5709-a268-9be5c6653c07" "ec96c562-7607-507f-9b9b-19e63a261a9a" "f3b901ef-66b6-5561-805a-3f02727212c2" "7b14ef7e-3f31-57b2-8f96-effeb4b7088d" "99fc5045-61f5-50fa-a0e2-8f0003e56fa4"] :answer-field/correct "f3b901ef-66b6-5561-805a-3f02727212c2" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "b6019cfe-9d9c-5e37-b6df-d53d3e14ef50" :question/id #uuid "b6019cfe-9d9c-5e37-b6df-d53d3e14ef50" :question/problem "Evaluate the triple integral\n\n$$\n\\iiint_R 2\\cdot x\\cdot z\\,\\mathrm{d}V\n$$\n\nover the region $R$ enclosed inside the cylinder $x^2+y^2=6$ for $y\\ge 0$ and between the surfaces $z=-x$ and $z=x+10.$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n\\iiint_R f(x,y,z)\\,dV=\\iiint_\\Delta f(r\\cos\\theta,r\\sin\\theta,z)\\,r\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta.\n$$\n\nIf $(r,\\theta,z)$ are the cylindrical polar coordinates of a point, then its Cartesian coordinates $(x,y,z)$ can be found by using the formulas\n\n$$\nx=r\\cos\\theta,\\quad y=r\\sin\\theta,\\quad z=z.\n$$\n\nFirst, let's sketch the projection of $R$ onto the $xy$-plane:\n\n![](images/04/0472caa4e40aac437429c5f542f8c7c155d69ff1a348e1d8a4c37b4ced9b472e.png)\n\nThe region $R$ is a right vertical cylinder of radius $\\sqrt{6}$ whose axis passes through the point $(0,0)$ in the $xy$-plane, and is\n\n- bounded below by $z=-x=-r\\cdot \\cos(\\theta),$ and\n\n- bounded above by $z=x+10=r\\cdot \\cos(\\theta)+10.$\n\nAs a result, in cylindrical polar coordinates, our region can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\Delta=\\{(r,\\theta,z):0\\le r\\le \\sqrt{6},\\ 0\\le\\theta<\\pi,\\ -r\\cdot \\cos(\\theta)\\le z\\le r\\cdot \\cos(\\theta)+10\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\iiint_R 2\\cdot x\\cdot z\\,dV &=\\iiint_\\Delta (2\\cdot z\\cdot r\\cdot \\cos(\\theta))\\cdot r\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{\\pi}\\int_0^{\\sqrt{6}}\\int_{-r\\cdot \\cos(\\theta)}^{r\\cdot \\cos(\\theta)+10}2\\cdot z\\cdot (r)^{2}\\cdot \\cos(\\theta)\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{\\pi}\\int_0^{\\sqrt{6}}(r)^{2}\\cdot \\cos(\\theta)[(z)^2]_{z=-r\\cdot \\cos(\\theta)}^{z=r\\cdot \\cos(\\theta)+10}\\,dr\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{\\pi}\\int_0^{\\sqrt{6}}(r)^{2}\\cdot \\cos(\\theta)((r\\cdot \\cos(\\theta)+10)^2-(-r\\cdot \\cos(\\theta))^2)\\,dr\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{\\pi}\\int_0^{\\sqrt{6}}(r)^{2}\\cdot \\cos(\\theta)((r)^{2}\\cdot (\\cos(\\theta))^{2}+20\\cdot r\\cdot \\cos(\\theta)+100-((r)^{2}\\cdot (\\cos(\\theta))^{2}))\\,dr\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{\\pi}\\int_0^{\\sqrt{6}}20\\cdot (r)^{3}\\cdot (\\cos(\\theta))^{2}+100\\cdot (r)^{2}\\cdot \\cos(\\theta)\\,dr\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{\\pi}[5\\cdot (r)^{4}\\cdot (\\cos(\\theta))^{2}+\\frac{100}{3}\\cdot (r)^{3}\\cdot \\cos(\\theta)]_{r=0}^{r=\\sqrt{6}}\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{\\pi}(5\\cdot ((\\sqrt{6}))^{4}\\cdot (\\cos(\\theta))^{2})-(5\\cdot ((0))^{4}\\cdot (\\cos(\\theta))^{2})+(\\frac{100}{3}\\cdot ((\\sqrt{6}))^{3}\\cdot \\cos(\\theta))-(\\frac{100}{3}\\cdot ((0))^{3}\\cdot \\cos(\\theta))\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{\\pi}(180\\cdot (\\cos(\\theta))^{2})-(0)+(200\\cdot \\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\cos(\\theta))-(0)\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{\\pi}180\\cdot (\\cos(\\theta))^{2}+200\\cdot \\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\cos(\\theta)\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{\\pi}180(\\frac{1}{2}(1+\\cos(2\\cdot \\theta)))+200\\cdot \\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\cos(\\theta)\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{\\pi}200\\cdot \\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\cos(\\theta)+90\\cdot \\cos(2\\cdot \\theta)+90\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=[90\\cdot \\theta+200\\cdot \\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\sin(\\theta)+45\\cdot \\sin(2\\cdot \\theta)]_{\\theta=0}^{\\theta=\\pi} \\\\ &=(90\\cdot \\pi)-(0)+(0)-(0)+(0)-(0) \\\\ &=90\\cdot \\pi\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["1b4a19c6-9237-53cb-b88d-eea0421ee991"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "generator" :question-generator/id #uuid "6edc76bd-ad65-59af-b3e7-ddae1eac78b5" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186129